#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# differential_leader

#% text
# `differential_leader(p, u, x)` gives the leader of the differential polynomial `p` in the functions `u` (a name or a list) of `x` (a name or a list): the derivative of highest rank that occurs in `p`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The ranking is `ranking: orderly` (the default: derivatives of higher total order rank higher, then the earlier function of the list `u`, then the multi-index lexicographically) or `ranking: elimination` (every derivative of an earlier function ranks above every derivative of a later one).

#% item
# Differential polynomials are polynomials in the functions and their derivatives with coefficients rational in the independent variables. The result is `none` when `p` contains no derivative of the functions.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
differential_leader(derivative(1, 0)(u)(x, t)^2 - 4*u(x, t)*derivative(0, 1)(u)(x, t), u, [x, t])
#% output
#= derivative(1, 0)(u)(x, t)

#% text
# Orderly and elimination rankings:

#% cell
differential_leader(y'(x) + z''(x)*y(x), [y, z], x)
#% output
#= z''(x)

#% cell
differential_leader(y'(x) + z(x)*y(x), [y, z], x, ranking: elimination)
#% output
#= y'(x)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `differential_initial`, `differential_separant`, `differential_reduce`, `rosenfeld_groebner`
